<div class="page">

<header>
  <p class="eyebrow">Unified platform &middot; reference</p>
  <h1>Two Modes, One Board</h1>
  <p class="lede">FastSim can build the same AE350 board two different ways. One of them puts every device on a SystemC bus; the other keeps every device inside QEMU. Only the first has anything a second CPU could share &mdash; and it is the one that already matches vsim.</p>
</header>

<h2>The difference in one picture</h2>
<p class="sub">Who owns the address map is the whole distinction. Everything else follows from it.</p>

<figure>
<svg viewBox="0 0 940 300" role="img" aria-label="In -M none mode the QEMU CPU and the SystemC router share one address map holding every device. In -M andes_ae350 mode the QEMU machine holds every device and only a small bridged window reaches the SystemC router.">
